/-
Suggested Lean forms for the roadmap
"Adic Spaces PartII, Part II: rigid-analytic Zariski geometry, classical points and resolution".

This file is not the roadmap and is not exhaustive: the roadmap document
(`research/blueprint/readmes/AdicSpacesPartIIPartII.md`) is definitive. The statements below suggest
Lean forms so that contributors and reviewers converge on names and signatures. Every proof is
`sorry`; nothing here is an implementation.

Only what is easily stated at the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti is stated here: the commutative algebra
behind nowhere density, the matrix-minor description of rank loci, the residue-field fact behind
the Gauss point theorem, and the analytic statements of the last layer (inverse function theorem,
constant rank theorem, identity theorem across a subfield), all on Mathlib carriers. Rigid spaces,
their Zariski closed subsets, normalizations, irreducible components, singular loci, Shilov points,
rigid blow-ups and resolutions have no carrier at the pins; they are README targets, listed at the
end of the file.
-/
